<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · mountain</p><h1 class="enc-title">Cal Madow</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Cal Madow is a mountain range in northern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/somalia">Somalia</a>, running east to west near the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gulf-of-aden">Gulf of Aden</a> coast, mainly in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sanaag">Sanaag</a> region and into <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bari">Bari</a>. Its highest point, Shimbiris, at about 2,400 metres, is the highest mountain in Somalia. The range holds juniper forests and frankincense and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/myrrh">myrrh</a> trees, whose resins were long traded through ports such as <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/las-khorey">Las Khorey</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/cal-madow.jpg" alt="Cal Madow" width="320" height="240" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Abdirisak · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Almadow_Overview.JPG" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
